{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405114-just-bought-book-of-the-fallen-hermetic-demonoligist-question","id":1405114,"title":"Just bought Book of the Fallen - Hermetic Demonoligist question.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-28T19:20:21-07:00","id":1405114,"title":"Just bought Book of the Fallen - Hermetic Demonoligist question.","content":"Ok, after I made my Imp thread, and reading some of the replies, I used my old Drive Thru account to pick up M20 BotF. It looks good, but now I\u2019m seriously considering getting back into Mage, and I\u2019m curious about a few things. First of all, why would my Hermetic Demonoligist become a Demonoligist when angels out number demons 2-1? Could it be that demons go out of their way to make themselves more approachable and useful than angels so more people will turn to them for help, thus increasing their chances to market damnation? I remember in the Rev OoH book that an angel was about to disembowel a young apprentice for forgetting minor formalities. It might be helpful/hilarious if word got around that not only do demons offer better deals than Above, but it is also actually safer to summon them since they WANT repeat business and their business is spread word of mouth. \u201cTell your friends!\u201d<br /> <br /> Anyways, why become a Demonoligist unless you are simply training to kill demons, like a Celestial Choruser? What sort of juice can I get for my squeeze in the OoH that would make binding and summoning demons more worthwhile than angels? I\u2019m not necessarily looking to make this like Exalted, where the solution to every problem can be found in Summon Demon of the 1st-3rd Circle, but it is worth thinking about. It is supposed to be tempting, after all, and a scary path to power that you can theoretically handle with sufficient magical expertise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T21:28:15-07:00","id":1405125,"title":"","content":"Alrighty so bearing in mind this response is done with the resources of my own memory and tried to fit the paradigm at hand, as well as just being my own opinions.<br /> <br /> \u2022Why Demons?<br /> Demons get shit done and don't ask troublesome questions.<br /> <br /> That's the long and short of it I imagine. One doesn't go to demons as the first choice unless they must. Angels are more powerful, by and large. Djinn are more personable, by and large. Umbrood are more versatile, by and large. Why then, demons, who are notoriously treacherous and hungry for your soul?<br /> <br /> Well the demon doesn't asks why exactly you need the skull of a virgin. It just asks that you profane the name of a saint in return for the morbid object's retrieval. Fairly innocuous right? Particularly if you weren't overly religious anyway. Demons are unscrupulous and their rates are almost miraculous - why not?<br /> <br /> Demons WANT to work with you. A demon will go out of its way to offer the best services available and get you to come back. Demons are willing to get you nearly anything and unless you ask for something big they're wants are fairly reasonable or paltry.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's their game. Because people start to notice when you have a whiff of sulfur about you and they begin to avoid you. Demons begin asking for things in return. They want things that make you sick but... the rates are really, really good. It's just a one-time thing, no big deal right?<br /> <br /> Sure it isn't. Not until you wake up rubbing ram's blood against your nipples and the sounds of an infernal host screaming past you to wreck havoc in the local suburbs. Oops.<br /> <br /> As for what you can get out of it?<br /> <br /> Aside from Dark Gifts, Dark Thaumaturgy, Infernal Boons, and the like; you get whatever the hosts of Hell can offer and all without the fear of the Heavenly Host hanging over your head like a Damocles Sword.<br /> <br /> If you want the angel to heed your call you had best be armed with names, words of power, protective amulets, and ritual purification. You'd want most of that Witt demons too, but an incubus is less likely to smite you for the mere act of summoning it.<br /> <br /> After all - bad for business.<br /> <br /> In general though, the Order of Hermes teaches its acolytes to deal with the Lower Powers very carefully. Compelling a demon into service and dealing with it from a position of power is acceptable. So long as your Will remains supreme and you can deal from a position of power, the Order will simply caution careful practice.<br /> <br /> It's when you've begun to dance the fiend's dance, heed their calls, and become reliant upon their power instead of your own Will that you've crossed the line into Infernalism and have become a threat to not only yourself but the Order as a whole.<br /> <br /> Pray that night never comes - and that Angels never feel the need to visit you of their own accord and on their own business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T06:46:36-07: