one of them will gladly kill you for forgetting protocol. I\u2019m kind of understanding why the Nephandi are a thing now. Even imps can make better friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T09:55:27-07:00","id":1405175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405114-just-bought-book-of-the-fallen-hermetic-demonoligist-question?p=1405155#post1405155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait angels (that interact with humanity on any level) are a thing in WoD?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the High/Astral Umbra every concept humanity has ever thought of is a thing. From the archangel Michael to Optimus Prime the transformer. But thanks to his millennia long association with Abrahamic religion the former will have a lot more raw power behind him than the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T10:14:50-07:00","id":1405176,"title":"","content":"If you want to get more into the gnostic side of angels check out Blood Treachery, it has a section devoted to the OoH and their angel allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T10:25:43-07:00","id":1405177,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, the old 'High umbra' trick. (which I honestly thought was never used) <br /> <br /> So, not Gods servants, humanity's imagination of God's servants. Was a bit shocked there. <br /> Even then, I didn't know you could really deal with high umbral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T10:53:22-07:00","id":1405180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405114-just-bought-book-of-the-fallen-hermetic-demonoligist-question?p=1405177#post1405177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes, the old 'High umbra' trick. (which I honestly thought was never used) <br /> <br /> So, not Gods servants, humanity's imagination of God's servants. Was a bit shocked there. <br /> Even then, I didn't know you could really deal with high umbral entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>That definition opens up a can of worms however, was Caine cursed by non existent humanities imagination of Angel's? What does that make the Fallen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T11:30:36-07:00","id":1405183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405114-just-bought-book-of-the-fallen-hermetic-demonoligist-question?p=1405175#post1405175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the High/Astral Umbra every concept humanity has ever thought of is a thing. From the archangel Michael to Optimus Prime the transformer (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could such Decepticons be natural allies of the Nephandi? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T13:14:29-07:00","id":1405189,"title":"","content":"Well the things in the High Umbra aren't really any less real then the things in the Middle or Lower Umbra - so if one accepts incarna and ferrymen then by necessity one must also accept the platonic ideal of the Archangel Raphael and the classic Peanuts\u2122 character Snoopy.<br /> <br /> Are the Angels of the Higher Umbra the same Angels that DtF refers to? No, I personally don't think so - although DtF's Angels probably reside closer to the Higher Umbra. However just because these aren't the Angels of the seven houses doesn't mean that the various heavens of the Higher Umbra are any less real on a practical level.<br /> <br /> As real as anything in the Umbra can be which is certainly a question for the Awakened to mull over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T15:37:11-07:00","id":1405206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405114-just-bought-book-of-the-fallen-hermetic-demonoligist-question?p=1405189#post1405189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the things in the High Umbra aren't really any less real then the things in the Middle or Lower Umbra - so if one accepts incarna and ferrymen then by necessity one must also accept the platonic ideal of the Archangel Raphael and the classic Peanuts\u2122 character Snoopy.<br /> <br /> Are the Angels of the Higher Umbra the same Angels that DtF refers to? No, I personally don't think so - although DtF's Angels probably reside closer to the Higher Umbra. However just because these aren't the Angels of the seven houses doesn't mean that the various heavens of the Higher Umbra are any less real on a practical level.</div> </div> </div> </div>DtF's Angels (or a very similar metaphysical species), according to dev commentary on <i>Ascension</i>, dwell beyond the Far Horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T02:57:26-07:00","id":1405283,"title":"","content":"Given how difficult &amp; dangerous summoning angles can be, I imagine that Hermetics that do it successfully gain significant social status from the feat. <br /> <br /> Also a great way to show up a Choruser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.