ink":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:23:29-07:00","id":1406093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1405114-just-bought-book-of-the-fallen-hermetic-demonoligist-question?p=1405847#post1405847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the Order of a Herm\u00e8s are elitist fucks that try to control everything, and wants to rule over sleepers</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not even though. If anything, the OoH have the Umbrella paradigm that encompasses all other paradigms which allows for them to co-operate best with any other tradition. A mage of the OoH, through their very broad paradigm, can understand what any other tradition or technocrat is doing. A Verbenna can't make a lick of sense of what an etherite is doing, or what a chorister is doing, or what an akashic is doing, though they might have a small understanding of what the chak's are doing; A Hermetic mage can look at all those things and grasp what's actually going on to a good degree. They might get a little proud of this or a little frustrated that the other traditions aren't seeing the bigger picture, but they are the glue that keeps the Traditions as Traditions rather than Disparates 1.0. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"